.TH LINKWISE-MODEMD 1 "2026-11-12" "Linkwise" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linkwise\-modemd \- run and diagnose a Linkwise software modem station
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linkwise\-modemd
.RB { \-h | \-\-help | \-\-version | \-\-audio\-devices | \-\-simulate }
.br
.B linkwise\-modemd
.RB { \-\-check\-config | \-\-check\-station | \-\-serve\-station }
.I FILE
.br
.B linkwise\-modemd \-\-simulate\-audio
.I PROFILE
.br
.B linkwise\-modemd \-\-serve\-bench
.IR CALL " [" CONTROL_PORT " " DATA_PORT ]
.br
.B linkwise\-modemd \-\-serve\-virtual\-bw500
.IR CALL " " PROFILE " [" CONTROL_PORT " " DATA_PORT " " AUDIO_PORT ]
.br
.B linkwise\-modemd \-\-serve\-virtual\-wide
.IR CALL " " BANDWIDTH " [" CONTROL_PORT " " DATA_PORT " " AUDIO_PORT ]
.br
.B linkwise\-modemd \-\-virtual\-audio\-device
.I AUDIO_PORT INPUT_DEVICE OUTPUT_DEVICE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a native audio station, check a station configuration, or exercise the
modem in a radio-free bench session.
Select one operation per invocation.
The packaged audio build uses 48 kHz audio.
Station and bench listeners bind to IPv4 loopback.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-audio\-devices
List the available capture and playback device names.
.TP
.BI "\-\-check\-config " FILE
Validate the station JSON and any referenced BW500 waveform profile.
.TP
.BI "\-\-check\-station " FILE
Validate the configuration, wait for capture samples, check the advertised
output format, and temporarily reserve the command and data ports.
This check plays no audio.
.TP
.BI "\-\-serve\-station " FILE
Run the station in the foreground.
A configured bandwidth enables transmit and receive using the configured
devices and separate command and data sockets.
Without a bandwidth, the command socket returns receive diagnostics as JSON.
The station handles SIGINT and SIGTERM.
.TP
.B \-\-simulate
Run a local modem exchange using simulated devices.
.TP
.BI "\-\-simulate\-audio " PROFILE
Run a local exchange using synthesized BW500 waveforms and the specified
measurement profile.
.TP
.BI "\-\-serve\-bench " CALL
Serve a simulated echo peer.
The default command and data ports are 8300 and 8301.
Supply both ports to override them.
.TP
.BI "\-\-serve\-virtual\-bw500 " "CALL PROFILE"
Serve a BW500 bench station with a TCP waveform cable.
The default command, data, and waveform ports are 8300, 8301, and 8302.
Supply all three ports to override them.
.TP
.BI "\-\-serve\-virtual\-wide " "CALL BANDWIDTH"
Serve a waveform cable station at 2300 or 2750 Hz.
Port arguments follow the same rules as for
.BR \-\-serve\-virtual\-bw500 .
.TP
.BI "\-\-virtual\-audio\-device " "AUDIO_PORT INPUT_DEVICE OUTPUT_DEVICE"
Bridge a local waveform socket to the selected capture and playback devices
on channel zero.
Use independent audio routes for an isolated test.
.SH OPERANDS
.I FILE
is a station JSON file described in
.BR linkwise-station (5).
.I PROFILE
is a BW500 measurement profile in JSON.
.I CALL
is the local station callsign.
Quote device names containing spaces.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The operation succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
An operation failed, including an invalid file or an audio or socket error.
.TP
.B 2
The command line did not select a recognized operation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
linkwise-modemd --audio-devices
linkwise-modemd --check-config station.json
linkwise-modemd --check-station station.json
linkwise-modemd --serve-station station.json
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR linkwise-station (5)
